#. type: Title =
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-pack-redundant.adoc:2
#, no-wrap
msgid "git-pack-redundant(1)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title -
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-pack-redundant.adoc:5
#, no-wrap
msgid "NAME"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-pack-redundant.adoc:7
msgid "git-pack-redundant - Find redundant pack files"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title -
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-pack-redundant.adoc:10
#, no-wrap
msgid "SYNOPSIS"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-pack-redundant.adoc:13
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"\t'git pack-redundant' [--verbose] [--alt-odb] (--all | "
"<pack-filename>...)\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title -
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-pack-redundant.adoc:15
#, no-wrap
msgid "WARNING"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-pack-redundant.adoc:21
msgid ""
"`git pack-redundant` has been deprecated and is scheduled for removal in a "
"future version of Git. Because it can only remove entire duplicate packs and "
"not individual duplicate objects, it is generally not a useful tool for "
"reducing repository size. You are better off using `git gc` to do so, which "
"will put objects into a new pack, removing duplicates."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-pack-redundant.adoc:27
msgid ""
"Running `pack-redundant` without the `--i-still-use-this` flag will fail in "
"this release. If you believe you have a use case for which `pack-redundant` "
"is better suited and oppose this removal, please contact the Git mailing "
"list at git@vger.kernel.org. More information about the list is available at "
"https://git-scm.com/community."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title -
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-pack-redundant.adoc:29
#, no-wrap
msgid "DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-pack-redundant.adoc:33
msgid ""
"This program computes which packs in your repository are redundant. The "
"output is suitable for piping to `xargs rm` if you are in the root of the "
"repository."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-pack-redundant.adoc:38
msgid ""
"'git pack-redundant' accepts a list of objects on standard input. Any "
"objects given will be ignored when checking which packs are required. This "
"makes the following command useful when wanting to remove packs which "
"contain unreachable objects."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-pack-redundant.adoc:41
msgid ""
"git fsck --full --unreachable | cut -d ' ' -f3 | \\ git pack-redundant --all "
"| xargs rm"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title -
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-pack-redundant.adoc:43
#, no-wrap
msgid "OPTIONS"
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-pack-redundant.adoc:46
#, no-wrap
msgid "`--all`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-pack-redundant.adoc:48
msgid "Processes all packs. Any filenames on the command line are ignored."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-pack-redundant.adoc:49
#, no-wrap
msgid "`--alt-odb`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-pack-redundant.adoc:52
msgid ""
"Don't require objects present in packs from alternate object database (odb) "
"directories to be present in local packs."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-pack-redundant.adoc:53
#, no-wrap
msgid "`--verbose`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-pack-redundant.adoc:55
msgid "Outputs some statistics to stderr. Has a small performance penalty."
msgstr ""

